        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=30^{\\circ},\\ 330^{\\circ}$.",
          "worked": "Cosine is the $x$-coordinate. The unit-circle points with $x=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ are in quadrants I and IV.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\theta&=30^{\\circ}\\text{ or }360^{\\circ}-30^{\\circ}\\\\\\theta&=30^{\\circ}\\text{ or }330^{\\circ}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 0,
        "responseSpace": "scaffold"
      },
      {
        "id": "p37-q2-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\sin\\theta=\\frac{1}{2}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=30^{\\circ},\\ 150^{\\circ}$.",
          "worked": "Sine is the $y$-coordinate. The unit-circle points with $y=\\frac{1}{2}$ are in quadrants I and II.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\theta&=30^{\\circ}\\text{ or }180^{\\circ}-30^{\\circ}\\\\\\theta&=30^{\\circ}\\text{ or }150^{\\circ}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p37-q2-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\sin\\theta=-\\frac{1}{2}$",
